.TH UNITWHY 1
.SH NAME
unitwhy \- collect systemd unit state and hardening evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unitwhy
--unit UNIT [--journal-lines COUNT] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Queries systemd for a unit's active state, result, execution status, unit file,
drop-ins, selected resource controls, and selected hardening settings. It can
also include a bounded tail of that unit's journal. The command is read-only and
reports partial visibility when systemd or journal access is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --unit UNIT
Systemd unit name to inspect.
.TP
.B --journal-lines COUNT
Include zero through 200 recent journal lines; the default is 20.
.TP
.B --format json
Emit the versioned JSON report (the only supported format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means the unit is active with a successful result; 1 means a failed unit or
failed result; 2 invalid usage; 3 partial or non-active evidence; and 4 a
collector runtime failure.
